    "title": "Viral US$93b US Department of War spending claim draws scrutiny; Singapore falls short in global city authenticity rankings: Singapore live news",
    "text": "Claims about spending on seafood and other luxury food items by the United States Department of War (formerly Department of Defence) circulated widely online after watchdog groups highlighted procurement entries in federal databases. Media reports pointed to purchases such as lobster, crab legs and steak listed in government contract records. One widely shared claim alleged the Pentagon spent US$93 billion in a single month under Pentagon chief Pete Hegseth, citing procurement data that gained traction on social media and in news coverage.A fact-check by Snopes said the US$93 billion figure reflected total obligations recorded in procurement systems rather than discretionary spending on specific items (Snopes). Reports citing watchdog analysis also pointed to US$22 million spent on steak and lobster in one month and about US$9 million on crab legs and lobster over several months, based on procurement records across military facilities. Additional entries such as fruit baskets and a Japanese flute appeared in contract records, which form part of the Pentagon’s extensive procurement system supplying food and other goods to bases, ships and overseas operations.A global ranking based on more than 1.3 million traveller reviews placed Singapore among the world’s least authentic cities, trailing Chicago, Venice, Sydney and Hobart. The study analysed review language, including terms like “authentic,” “local” and “tourist trap,” to assign an authenticity score out of 100, with Singapore scoring low due to perceptions of commercialised tourist areas.Experts note that even cities ranked as less authentic can offer meaningful experiences if travellers explore beyond the main attractions. Local consultants highlight spots like Tiong Bahru, Kampong Glam and hawker centres, where traditional charm persists despite the city’s commercialised shopping districts. While the ranking focuses on perceived cultural authenticity, Singapore continues to excel in safety, cleanliness and efficiency, and travellers can still find authentic encounters with careful planning.Read more in our live blog below, including the latest local and international news and updates.Live coverage is over13 updates",
